{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Ba-gad.</b> Two words, and the alef is missing. So too in all [such cases], and so too במה (Ezekiel 20:29), as is explained in Ezekel." "<b>The meaning of גָד גְּדוּד:</b> for she has a troop (גְּדוּד) of sons. Others say that גד means a good fortune, as it is in the language of Ishmael, and like it: \"those who lay a table for גד\" (Isaiah 65:11), and it is the star Gad. The correct interpretation is that it is like גְּדוּדֵי הַשָּׁמַיִם:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "Reading 'וכן בכל וכן במה' as 'so too in all, and so too ba-mah'; the referent of 'in all' is uncertain—possibly all instances of this defective spelling.", 1 "Resolved 'וי״א' as ויש אומרים, 'others say'; resolved the Isaiah citation to 65:11 based on the verse content; the final phrase echoes Jeremiah 33:22."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:46:24.522128232Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}